      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is how it is handled on depthcharge side: https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/depthcharge/src/drivers/input/mkbp/mkbp.c?q\u003dmkbp+file:%5Esrc/platform/depthcharge/+package:%5Echromeos_public$\u0026g\u003d0\u0026l\u003d45\n\nCONFIG_DRIVER_INPUT_MKBP_NO_INTERRUPT is defined for all x86 boards. But fixing this on depthcharge side won\u0027t be just removing this config. Instead, cros_ec_interrupt_pending will have to be provided which queries gpe_sts to indicate if interrupt was actually triggered.",
